# Plan handover

This directory hands over {{ handover.plans | length }} plan{{ "s" if handover.plans | length != 1 }} and every item in them. Each item is one
pull request's worth of work: what it does, where it stands, what it builds on and what
is already known about it.

{% include "plan_handover_summary.md.jinja" %}

## What you need first

- **Write access to the repositories the items' branches and pull requests are on:**
{% for repository in handover.plans | map(attribute="manifest") | map(attribute="repositories") | sum(start=[]) | unique(attribute="full_name") %}
  [{{ repository.full_name }}]({{ repository.url }}){{ "," if not loop.last else "." }}
{% endfor %}
  The work in progress lives on branches there, so continuing it means pushing to them.
- **The project's own rules:** its `AGENTS.md` (else `CLAUDE.md`), and the standing rules
  of each plan below{% if handover.repository_rules.rules %} and of the repository, in
  [`{{ location.REPOSITORY_RULES }}`]({{ location.REPOSITORY_RULES }}){% endif %}. They bind every item as much as its own notes.

The sessions that started these items are left out: only the person who ran a session can
open it. What they decided is in each item's notes, its progress note and its pull request.

## Taking it over with basstler

basstler tracks the plans for you: dependency readiness, stacked pull requests, the plan
site and the progress notes. Set it up once, as its `docs/SETUP.md` describes, in a
checkout of your fork of the project, or of the repository above if you push to it.
Then, from that checkout:

```bash
basstler plan-handover import
```

That finds the handover pull request open on the repository (or, given this directory,
reads it from here). Plans whose repository is not your checkout's move onto it, with
the items already underway still naming the repository their pull requests are on. It
saves every plan, progress note and rule onto your own personal-notes branch. Start an
item that has not started with `/plan-item-kickoff <plan-id> <item-id>`, and continue one
that is underway with `/plan-item-resolve <plan-id> <item-id>`; both read everything below
for you.

## Taking it over without basstler

Work one item per session. Give Claude Code, or yourself, this prompt with the item's
section of this guide pasted below it:

```text
Work the plan item below. Before changing anything:
1. Read the project's AGENTS.md (else CLAUDE.md) and the plan's standing rules in this guide.
2. If the item has a branch, check it out and build on what is on it; read its pull request,
   its description and every unresolved review thread, and its progress note in this guide's
   pr-progress directory.
3. If it has no branch, cut one from the branch of the dependency it stacks on that has not
   merged yet, else from the default branch, and open a draft pull request.
4. Read the comments on the plan's tracking issue: structural changes to the plan are posted there.
Then plan the change with tests first, implement it, and keep the pull request's description
and the progress note true to the work.
```

The plans come after the plans they depend on. Each item links the items it depends on:
start it once they have merged, or stack it on the branch of the one that has not.

